This "minishell" was a  C project intended to familiarize myself more with the inner workings of a shell. It features a few custom command implementations, while using fork and execvp to do the remainder, implements an interrupt handler for SIGINT (ctrl + C), and features some error handling.

Custom commands are as follows: (Attempting to input too many arguments will result in an error)
* cd [directory] - changes the current directory to [directory]. A ~ will expand to your home directory! 
* pwd - prints the current working directory
* lf - lists every file and directory in your current working directory, excluding . and ..
* lp - lists all currently running processes by reading /proc sorted by their PID! Owner and the command are also listed.  
* exit - exits minishell
